From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 03:13:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] winemetal/airconv: runtime control bridge, capture aspect
 copies, budget trim, GPU timing, defined render-target output lanes

MadeiraCtl (slot 138): capture polling, file writes into the sandbox, config
lookups and command-buffer GPU start/end times for the runtime's perf census.
Texture-to-buffer blits carry an options field so depth and stencil aspect
copies skip the block-compressed pitch check. The advertised video budget can
be held fixed (vram-trim-mb = 0): a moving budget made the streamer thrash.
Configuration comes from one file through madeira_cfg.h.

airconv: a pixel shader that writes only some lanes of a render-target output
used to shuffle the others in as undef, and LLVM folded the blend equation
around an undefined source alpha to a constant 0. Unwritten lanes are now
(0,0,0,1), the convention of the hardware D3D titles ship against. Also:
interpolants the paired vertex stage never writes are zero-filled instead of
rejecting the pipeline; SM5.x DXBC through the public converter entry.

Madeira-commit: 4c86e0920cea26d32d195429ae79644be7f41a03
Rebased: resolved
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-dxmt-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
